/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://gzijmkzwnfebgaqxcrbh.supabase.co; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built from what Kitchen actually loads, checked against the source:
#
#   script-src 'self'      the built index.html has no inline script — Vite
#                          emits one same-origin module and one stylesheet
#   style-src  'unsafe-inline'
#                          REQUIRED, and the one loose directive here. There
#                          are 110 `style={{…}}` attributes across the screens,
#                          and CSP blocks inline style attributes without it.
#                          Removing it is a real refactor, not a header edit.
#   img-src    https:      recipe `image_url` is a link Lexi pastes, so it can
#                          be any host. No recipe uses one today; the field is
#                          there, and a silently blank image would be a
#                          confusing bug. Images can't execute.
#   connect-src            Supabase REST only. Kitchen uses no realtime, so no
#                          wss: is needed — verified, not assumed.
#   frame-src  youtube     RecipeDetail embeds https://www.youtube.com/embed/…
#                          for the how-it's-made video.
#   no font-src beyond self, no data:, no worker-src — nothing uses them.
#
# ENFORCING as of 2026-09-01, in a second deploy after the report-only one.
# Cleared first in two independent passes: locally against the built bundle
# with the policy enforcing (13 routes, plus positive and negative controls —
# a jsdelivr script blocked, proving it wasn't silently inert), then on the
# live site report-only as admin and as guest. Zero violations in all of them.
#
# If a screen ever breaks after a change here, put `-Report-Only` back on the
# header name and redeploy — that's the whole rollback.
#
# The other four headers are enforcing from the start — they can't break a
# screen the way a wrong CSP can.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
